Where the code came from
------------------------

The launcher is derived from MyChrome by cnjackchen
(https://github.com/cnjackchen/my-chrome), which is licensed GPL-3.0. That project is
the origin of the AutoIt design: the update-check pipeline, the portable folder layout
and the settings model.

The 3.8.x line was published as MyBrowser by xixiranran
(https://github.com/xixiranran/MyChrome) as compiled binaries only — no source was
published there. The source in src/ was recovered from that 3.8.50 release, then
modernised here from 3.9.0 onward.

Both are GPL-3.0, so this derivative is GPL-3.0. The complete corresponding source for
every release is in this repository and attached to each release as a _source.7z archive.

Changes made here since 3.9.0
-----------------------------

Chrome now resolves through Chrome for Testing with a direct ZIP install; Firefox,
Chromium, Brave and Vivaldi download sources were repaired or added; the update engine
gained integrity checks, temp cleanup, a skip-this-version option and a support log;
hardcoded Google API credentials were removed; --no-sandbox was dropped from the
defaults; command injection in the DLL-injection path was fixed.

Bundled third-party components
------------------------------

Each keeps its own licence; see licenses/ for texts where they are redistributable.

  7z.exe, 7z.dll                       7-Zip, GNU LGPL with the unRAR restriction
  GreenChrome*.dll, setdll*.exe        GreenChrome / Microsoft setdll
  mozlz4-win*.exe                      MozLz4, MPL-2.0
  MouseInc.*, hook*.dll                MouseInc
  TabPlus.*                            TabPlus

Chrome, Chromium, Edge, Brave, Firefox, Vivaldi and every other browser named in this
repository are downloaded from their vendors at runtime and are not redistributed here.
